      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for the tip. so if the \"flexibility\" argument was mostly just a tactic by elites, does that mean we should basically view the entire history of anti-union legislation as an attempt to undermine democracy itself? it feels like there wasn't really a \"valid\" side to the businesses' concerns if their goal was just to protect profits at the expense of the people.",
